  "step_3": "The decision reason requires comparing the probability of the maximum outcome — that is, the probability of receiving the non-zero amount. The individual instead focused on the probability of receiving 0 Euros, which is the complement of the maximum outcome probability. While the individual’s observation is factually correct (66% vs. 67%), they did not apply or reference the rule that prefers the lottery with the higher probability of the maximum outcome. There is no mention of comparing the 33% vs. 34% probabilities of achieving 2500 or 2400 Euros. Therefore, the individual did not use the specified decision reason. The information considered (probability of zero outcome) is related but not equivalent to the information required by the decision reason. The justification also does not reflect the rule of the reason. Thus, the decision reason was not used.",
  "final_assessment_score": 0
